ation of breast cancer resistance protein (BCRP/ABCG2) gene expression using RNA interference</article-title><source>Mol Cancer Ther</source><year>2004b</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>1577</fpage><lpage>1583</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Mol Cancer Ther||3|1577||bib10|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15634651</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ee</surname><given-names>PLR</given-names></name><name><surname>Kamalakaran</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Tonetti</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>He</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Ross</surname><given-names>DD</given-names></name><name><surname>Beck</surname><given-names>WT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Identification of a novel estrogen response element in the breast cancer resistance protein (ABCG2) gene</article-title><source>Cancer Res</source><year>2004a</year><volume>64</volume><fpage>1247</fpage><lpage>1251</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer Res||64|1247||bib11|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14973083</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ferlini</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Raspaglio</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Mozzetti</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Distefano</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Filippetti</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Martinelli</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Ferrandina</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Gallo</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Ranelletti</surname><given-names>FO</given-names></name><name><surname>Scambia</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bcl-2 down-regulation is a novel mechanism of paclitaxel resistance</article-title><source>Mol Pharmacol</source><year>2003</year><volume>64</volume><fpage>51</fpage><lpage>58</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Mol Pharmacol||64|51||bib12|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12815160</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Foster</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Ho</surname><given-names>YT</given-names></name><name><surname>Newman</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name><name><surname>Kasprzyk</surname><given-names>PG</given-names></name><name><surname>Leese</surname><given-names>MP</given-names></name><name><surname>Potter</surname><given-names>BVL</given-names></name><name><surname>Reed</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Purohit</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>2-MeOE2<italic>bis</italic>MATE and 2-EtE2<italic>bis</italic>MATE induce cell cycle arrest and apoptosis in breast cancer xenografts as shown by a novel <italic>ex vivo</italic> technique</article-title><source>Breast Cancer Res Treat</source><year>2008</year><volume>111</volume><fpage>251</fpage><lpage>260</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Breast Cancer Res Treat||111|251||bib13|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17957467</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fotsis</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Pepper</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><name><surname>Adlercreutz</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Montesano</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Nawroth</surname><given-names>PP</given-names></name><name><surname>Schweigerer</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><articl